  "contract": "POST /api/system/repair/pass (published Server 2.11) runs one task repair pass: it recovers ready tasks that need redispatch and expired leases, creates missing workflow tasks, enforces expired run, activity and service-call deadlines, and reports each count with its failures, answering 207 when any failed. The pass is server-wide, so the fixture scopes every pass to run ids and a task queue that do not exist; each then reports zero candidates and echoes its trimmed filters, with empty strings read as null. Run ids are at most 100 non-empty strings; respect_throttle is a boolean; connection and queue are at most 128 characters. Invalid requests answer Laravel's 422. Embedded applications have no HTTP system routes."
